WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.820
- We are trying to start off 2021

00:00:01.820 --> 00:00:03.230
with strength and positivity.

00:00:03.230 --> 00:00:05.720
So all week I've been
talking about some authors

00:00:05.720 --> 00:00:08.800
I turn to when I need an emotional boost,

00:00:08.800 --> 00:00:11.370
some of the best inspirational
minds on the planet.

00:00:11.370 --> 00:00:14.240
People including Glennon
Doyle, DeVon Franklin

00:00:14.240 --> 00:00:15.560
and Brene Brown.

00:00:15.560 --> 00:00:19.050
Another one is the
great Dr. Deepak Chopra.

00:00:19.050 --> 00:00:22.460
He says, "Victims always
feel alone and helpless.

00:00:22.460 --> 00:00:25.227
Freedom from victimhood is creativity."

00:00:25.227 --> 00:00:26.950
"I could not agree more",

00:00:26.950 --> 00:00:29.490
says the creative person
sitting in front of you.

00:00:29.490 --> 00:00:30.600
I think we can all relate

00:00:30.600 --> 00:00:33.276
to feeling victimized by 2020, right?

00:00:33.276 --> 00:00:34.751
(applause)

00:00:34.751 --> 00:00:36.490
Yeah, it doesn't matter who
you are, it kind of sucked.

00:00:36.490 --> 00:00:40.913
But those, exactly, I got a amen!

00:00:40.913 --> 00:00:42.930
Well, those words completely ring true

00:00:42.930 --> 00:00:44.680
for Isa who's joining us today.

00:00:44.680 --> 00:00:47.740
2020 was really tough on you, right, Isa?

00:00:47.740 --> 00:00:50.670
- Yes, it was pretty tough.

00:00:50.670 --> 00:00:52.960
It started off super hopeful,

00:00:52.960 --> 00:00:56.960
but as the pandemic began

00:00:56.960 --> 00:00:59.240
I lost three jobs.

00:00:59.240 --> 00:01:01.060
I lost all my income

00:01:01.060 --> 00:01:03.720
and just a couple of weeks ago,

00:01:03.720 --> 00:01:06.973
one of my good friends,
lifelong friends passed away.

00:01:07.860 --> 00:01:12.860
I had to cancel my 30th
birthday trip to Belize

00:01:13.350 --> 00:01:16.430
and I am still living at home with my mom.

00:01:16.430 --> 00:01:21.430
So, to say that I feel
helpless is an understatement.

00:01:21.520 --> 00:01:26.520
And to feel like 2020
has diminished my hopes.

00:01:26.900 --> 00:01:29.480
So it just really sucks.

00:01:29.480 --> 00:01:30.860
- Yeah, you know what?

00:01:30.860 --> 00:01:32.410
Simply put, yep.

00:01:32.410 --> 00:01:35.790
But why does Deepak's
quote mean so much to you?

00:01:35.790 --> 00:01:37.760
Why does it hit home with you?

00:01:37.760 --> 00:01:39.530
- Because I'm feeling like a victim

00:01:39.530 --> 00:01:43.900
and we are all victims to this year.

00:01:43.900 --> 00:01:47.400
The circumstances have
forced that title on us.

00:01:47.400 --> 00:01:50.270
And so for his quote,

00:01:50.270 --> 00:01:51.890
I'm reminded that I have to rise

00:01:51.890 --> 00:01:54.810
above the circumstances
that I can't control.

00:01:54.810 --> 00:01:56.560
And I feel like we all need to rise

00:01:56.560 --> 00:01:59.640
above those circumstances
that we have no control over,

00:01:59.640 --> 00:02:01.740
especially for 2021.

00:02:01.740 --> 00:02:03.650
- Yeah, and for people
that are control freaks,

00:02:03.650 --> 00:02:04.973
that is hard.

00:02:06.320 --> 00:02:10.030
But good news though, we have
Deepak joining us this hour

00:02:10.030 --> 00:02:12.510
and not only is he going to
share his advice for Isa,

00:02:12.510 --> 00:02:15.870
he's also got suggestions
for how all of us

00:02:15.870 --> 00:02:19.190
can feel more empowered
to take on the world.

00:02:19.190 --> 00:02:21.150
'Cause it has felt really big lately.

00:02:21.150 --> 00:02:24.171
So it's nice to feel like
you got a grasp on something.

00:02:24.171 --> 00:02:28.290
So Dr. Chopra, you teamed up
with Oprah to help people cope

00:02:28.290 --> 00:02:30.848
with the stress we've
all faced lately, right?

00:02:30.848 --> 00:02:35.770
- Yes, so Oprah and I have
been teaching meditation online

00:02:35.770 --> 00:02:38.630
and we reached about 10 million people

00:02:38.630 --> 00:02:41.020
in the last few years.

00:02:41.020 --> 00:02:43.771
And right now we are
also engaging with people

00:02:43.771 --> 00:02:46.160
on a 21 day meditation experience

00:02:46.160 --> 00:02:48.780
called "Creating Peace
from the Inside Out",

00:02:48.780 --> 00:02:50.480
which is very important right now

00:02:50.480 --> 00:02:55.250
in times of turbulence and
so much ideological conflict.

00:02:55.250 --> 00:02:56.083
- That's great.

00:02:56.083 --> 00:02:57.670
Well, we already talked to Isa

00:02:57.670 --> 00:03:00.768
about how she can start 2021 right.

00:03:00.768 --> 00:03:02.510
But we also have some more people

00:03:02.510 --> 00:03:05.560
in the audience who could use
a little guidance as well.

00:03:05.560 --> 00:03:07.160
So let's start with Diamond.

00:03:07.160 --> 00:03:08.840
What's going on with you girl?

00:03:08.840 --> 00:03:11.340
- Yes, well, Kelly, I'll be honest.

00:03:11.340 --> 00:03:13.950
I've always been a super confident woman.

00:03:13.950 --> 00:03:15.950
Like, I'm the life of the party.

00:03:15.950 --> 00:03:17.210
When I step into a room,

00:03:17.210 --> 00:03:20.040
I am bringing so much positive energy.

00:03:20.040 --> 00:03:22.650
I'm a mom, I have my own
business doing social

00:03:22.650 --> 00:03:25.900
media management, I host events.

00:03:25.900 --> 00:03:28.370
And so with this year and
everything that's going on,

00:03:28.370 --> 00:03:31.010
it literally stopped, as we all know,

00:03:31.010 --> 00:03:34.930
and it totally knocked me off
my square, everything paused.

00:03:34.930 --> 00:03:36.630
And I was really left, feeling lost

00:03:36.630 --> 00:03:40.220
and angry and just really
not knowing what to do.

00:03:40.220 --> 00:03:42.272
I lost a lot of connections

00:03:42.272 --> 00:03:45.242
with people and I really thrive
off that human connection.

00:03:45.242 --> 00:03:49.040
Just trying to figure out
how to pivot my business

00:03:49.040 --> 00:03:51.510
in this time where it's
like so many events

00:03:51.510 --> 00:03:52.693
and getting out there.

00:03:53.670 --> 00:03:55.940
So I need to figure out how
do I get that confidence back?

00:03:55.940 --> 00:03:58.510
Find that confident,
strong woman that I know

00:03:58.510 --> 00:04:00.230
deep down inside that I am.

00:04:00.230 --> 00:04:01.920
So I can really continue to inspire

00:04:01.920 --> 00:04:03.340
my children, my daughters.

00:04:03.340 --> 00:04:05.340
And so I'm just trying to figure out

00:04:05.340 --> 00:04:06.173
where do I even begin with a year

00:04:06.173 --> 00:04:08.303
being so crazy and draining?

00:04:09.220 --> 00:04:10.880
- Well, maybe with that meditation thing

00:04:10.880 --> 00:04:13.179
he was just talking about,
but let's talk to Dr. Chopra.

00:04:13.179 --> 00:04:15.610
- One thing you can do instantly

00:04:15.610 --> 00:04:20.610
anytime you're stressed is use
what I call the stop formula.

00:04:21.300 --> 00:04:23.490
S-T-O-P.

00:04:23.490 --> 00:04:28.490
S stands for stop, T stands
for take three deep breaths

00:04:28.710 --> 00:04:32.518
and smile from your head
to your toes, everywhere.

00:04:32.518 --> 00:04:36.270
O, observe your breath
and your body sensations.

00:04:36.270 --> 00:04:40.540
And then P, proceed with
awareness, compassion, and joy.

00:04:40.540 --> 00:04:43.570
But what you're also doing,
which is very effective,

00:04:43.570 --> 00:04:45.760
is you're expressing your vulnerability.

00:04:45.760 --> 00:04:47.120
And that is very important.

00:04:47.120 --> 00:04:48.530
It's a sign of strength.

00:04:48.530 --> 00:04:51.450
When we express our
vulnerabilities to each other,

00:04:51.450 --> 00:04:53.099
we are stronger.

00:04:53.099 --> 00:04:55.510
So we ask for help and we give help.

00:04:55.510 --> 00:04:57.980
Social scientists these
days talk about something

00:04:57.980 --> 00:04:59.480
called the happiness formula,

00:04:59.480 --> 00:05:01.970
which is basically,
are you seeing problems

00:05:01.970 --> 00:05:04.130
or are you seeing opportunities?

00:05:04.130 --> 00:05:05.890
What are the conditions of your living?

00:05:05.890 --> 00:05:07.700
And do you have meaning and purpose?

00:05:07.700 --> 00:05:09.890
And can you make other people happy?

00:05:09.890 --> 00:05:12.430
The fastest way to
increase your self-esteem

00:05:12.430 --> 00:05:15.099
and be happy is to make
somebody else happy.

00:05:15.099 --> 00:05:17.440
- That's my favorite
thing that I've kind of

00:05:17.440 --> 00:05:20.270
heard people say in this
time, 'cause doing this show

00:05:20.270 --> 00:05:22.710
it's been absolutely a
blessing for me personally

00:05:22.710 --> 00:05:25.410
because you hear people
say, you know what,

00:05:25.410 --> 00:05:27.612
if you're having a hard time

00:05:27.612 --> 00:05:28.445
why don't you help someone else?

00:05:28.445 --> 00:05:30.635
Not only does it just
kind of take you away

00:05:30.635 --> 00:05:32.120
from your own egocentric
moment that you're suffering

00:05:32.120 --> 00:05:33.580
but you're focusing on
someone else, you help us

00:05:33.580 --> 00:05:34.710
and that makes you feel good.

00:05:34.710 --> 00:05:36.120
And it's so true.

00:05:36.120 --> 00:05:37.560
Do you feel like that?

00:05:37.560 --> 00:05:39.990
- Absolutely, I spent a
lot of my time doing that

00:05:39.990 --> 00:05:42.110
to make myself feel
better when I can't just

00:05:42.110 --> 00:05:44.100
make myself feel better.

00:05:44.100 --> 00:05:47.100
I find that if you're able
to help someone bridge

00:05:47.100 --> 00:05:50.240
that gap of trying to get to that spot,

00:05:50.240 --> 00:05:53.330
whether it's just having a
conversation or being able

00:05:53.330 --> 00:05:55.850
to help with this month's rent,

00:05:55.850 --> 00:05:57.890
or it's something as small as just being

00:05:57.890 --> 00:05:59.512
an ear to listen to.

00:05:59.512 --> 00:06:00.936
- Yeah.

00:06:00.936 --> 00:06:03.343
What do you think Nathan, does
any of that hit home for you?

00:06:04.220 --> 00:06:06.130
- I mean, first of all, I love this.

00:06:06.130 --> 00:06:07.890
Thank you very much for
everybody being here

00:06:07.890 --> 00:06:12.660
because it's not normal to sit and wallow

00:06:12.660 --> 00:06:15.480
in this kind of a stressful place.

00:06:15.480 --> 00:06:17.230
There's always another side.

00:06:17.230 --> 00:06:19.500
We always come out of
it on the other side.

00:06:19.500 --> 00:06:21.233
So I know it's there,

00:06:21.233 --> 00:06:23.830
but having the steps, having the guidance,

00:06:23.830 --> 00:06:26.780
having the try this, it's very comforting.

00:06:26.780 --> 00:06:28.293
- So Dr. Deepak, before we go,

00:06:28.293 --> 00:06:31.200
you just started a new
AI project that you kind

00:06:31.200 --> 00:06:33.440
of referenced and it sounds really cool.

00:06:33.440 --> 00:06:34.610
So can you tell us about it?

00:06:34.610 --> 00:06:37.260
'Cause you said it kind of,
it's an artificial intelligence

00:06:37.260 --> 00:06:38.930
but it also sets you up with other humans.

00:06:38.930 --> 00:06:40.230
Is that what you were saying?

00:06:40.230 --> 00:06:42.220
That kind of connect with people?

00:06:42.220 --> 00:06:43.510
How does it work?

00:06:43.510 --> 00:06:47.280
- I have an AI bot, which
is on neveralone.love,

00:06:47.280 --> 00:06:50.160
which can immediately assess
whether you're at risk

00:06:50.160 --> 00:06:53.840
for depression and can
befriend you and guide you

00:06:53.840 --> 00:06:57.056
and even connect you to
counselors and it's all free.

00:06:57.056 --> 00:06:59.650
- Oh my gosh, that's amazing!

00:06:59.650 --> 00:07:00.929
It's all free?

00:07:00.929 --> 00:07:02.440
- Yes.

00:07:02.440 --> 00:07:06.830
So check out, neveralone.love
and look for Piwi,

00:07:06.830 --> 00:07:10.920
she's the AI bot that can
become your best friend

00:07:10.920 --> 00:07:11.910
if you want.

00:07:11.910 --> 00:07:13.620
- Oh my God, that's really cool.

00:07:13.620 --> 00:07:16.320
Thank you so much for taking
the time everybody today.

